<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congress of Erfurt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1808</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Congress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erfurt">Erfurt</a> was a meeting between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I of Russia</a> held in Erfurt from 27 September to 14 October 1808, attended by many German princes. It was meant to renew the alliance agreed at Tilsit, but Alexander would not commit himself against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, encouraged in secret by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-maurice-de-talleyrand">Talleyrand</a>. During the congress Napoleon received Goethe in a famous audience.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congress-of-erfurt.jpg" alt="Congress of Erfurt" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nicolas Gosse · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entrevue_Erfurt_by_Nicolas_Grosse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
